UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Five of Pentacles represents the absolute archetype of "Systemic De-privation"—the harsh, high-intensity phase where the sovereign consciousness, having been too focused on conservation (the Four), encounters a external or internal reality where the lack of movement has led to a perceived or actual state of loss. Moving beyond the static security of the Four, the Five signifies the stage of "The Sovereign Survivor," where you are forced out of your bunker and into a state of vulnerability where your previous material definitions of "security" are stripped away. Visually depicted as two figures walking past a stained-glass window of a church, this archetype embodies the concept of "Sovereign Resilience"—the realization that true material mastery is not defined by what you possess, but by your ability to maintain your structural integrity even when the external manifest environment feels cold, barren, or hostile. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "Systemic Hardship," where you are being forced to confront the difference between your essential worth and your external assets. When the Five of Pentacles appears, your system is registering a "Resource Scarcity" status; you are feeling the pinch, and you are being invited to stop the "victim-narrative" of your circumstance and instead perform a brutal, diagnostic audit of your resource management. This card commands you to perform a brutal audit of your dependencies. You are being tasked with the essential work of "Intentional Adaptation": recognizing that the "church" (the solution or the support you think you need) is right there in your peripheral vision, and that the only thing keeping you from it is your own, pride-based refusal to ask for help or acknowledge your current, human reality. To inhabit the Five of Pentacles is to master the art of "Strategic Vulnerability," recognizing that by acknowledging your present need without egoic collapse, you are effectively initiating the necessary process of rebuilding your sovereign foundation from the ground up.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Five of Pentacles appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "Systemic Recovery," "The Turnaround," or the catastrophic—yet curative—transition out of the state of deprivation, leading to a state of slow, painful, yet deliberate, rebuilding of your material baseline. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates "lingering in the state of lack" with "being realistic," even as your actual, internal operating system is experiencing a vital, core-level restart. You are essentially "stepping out of the cold," running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to "stay in the safety of the known struggle" over the sober, unglamorous requirement to actually start the recovery. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the "permanently disenfranchised," while internally, you are being jolted by the realization that you have survived the worst, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency bewilderment, the experience of "not knowing who you are without the lack," and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your survival is the primary challenge you must now integrate. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of residual poverty-consciousness"; you are obsessively trying to analyze the damage, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final integration of your new baseline is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to fully recover, you would be forced to face the terrifying, blank-slate reality of your own, sovereign, and entirely responsible self. The reversed Five of Pentacles exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of "starting over," and the corresponding fear that if you were to drop the pretense of the "defeated survivor" and accept the gift of your survival, you would be forced to face the reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these post-collapse, lingering, lack-heavy scripts, perform a brutal audit of your recovery process, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize your potential over your history. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance stagnation, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of radical rebirth—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having prioritized the comfort of "the cold" over the vulnerability of "the warmth," and realizing that until you are willing to walk through the doors of the church (the support, the logic, the truth) and walk forward into the unknown reality of your own, new potential, you will continue to be starved by the very, phantom catastrophe you have worked so hard to simulate.'
WHERE id = 47;
